{
 "_comment": [
  "Measured Kernel-surface facts for michaelayoade/dotmac_platform_control_plane.",
  "MEASURED, not copied: an AST sweep over `git show <revision>:<path>` for every",
  "tracked *.py and *.pyprogram outside tests/, at the peeled revision below,",
  "using this repository's own `engine._kernel_imports` so the fixture and the",
  "engine cannot disagree about what an import binds. The .pyprogram entry is",
  "included deliberately -- it imports dotmac_kernel.db and is invisible to a",
  "suffix-based sweep.",
  "",
  "WHAT THIS FIXTURE IS, so no reader mistakes it for something else: a BOUNDED",
  "REGRESSION EXAMPLE. The acceptance proof for Platform's Kernel adoption is",
  "Platform #181's runner over Platform's LIVE source, in Platform's own CI,",
  "against a declaration Platform wrote. This file is 85 facts measured once at",
  "one pinned revision and replayed. Green here does not mean Platform is",
  "enrolled, and does not mean this still describes Platform's source.",
  "",
  "REGENERATED 2026-09-06 (second time), for `dmg-kernel-surface-v2`. Each fact",
  "now carries `bindings`: the Kernel's own name for a symbol and the local name",
  "the file bound it to, kept apart. `symbols` is the sorted distinct KERNEL half",
  "of `bindings` -- a projection, not a second record -- so the v1-shaped arms",
  "read exactly what they read before.",
  "",
  "The first regeneration, earlier the same day, was INCOMPLETE and this file",
  "said otherwise. It claimed every symbol was recorded as the Kernel spells it,",
  "and two of the three aliases were still stored under their LOCAL names:",
  "dotmac_kernel.messaging `models` was stored as `messaging_models`, and",
  "dotmac_kernel.migrations `versions_dir` as `kernel_versions_dir`. Only the",
  "root-facade alias was found, because the test that checked the convention",
  "only looked at facts whose module is the bare `dotmac_kernel`. Both are",
  "corrected here and both are in `known_aliases`.",
  "",
  "This is a FIXTURE and is labelled one. It carries Platform's measured Kernel",
  "surface and NOT Platform's source; the test synthesises import statements from",
  "`bindings`, so an aliased fact synthesises an ALIASED statement. Platform's own",
  "declaration is Platform's to write -- see the test module's docstring for",
  "exactly what this can and cannot demonstrate."
 ],
