  {
   "path": "alembic/env.py",
   "module": "dotmac_kernel.messaging",
   "kernel_name": "models",
   "local_name": "messaging_models",
   "note": "`from dotmac_kernel.messaging import models as messaging_models` on line 25, immediately above `from dotmac_kernel.models import Base` on line 26. The alias disambiguates the messaging package's `models` submodule from the Kernel's top-level `models`; both are names the Kernel publishes and neither is `messaging_models`."
  },
  {
   "path": "src/vendor_cp/migrations.py",
   "module": "dotmac_kernel.migrations",
   "kernel_name": "versions_dir",
   "local_name": "kernel_versions_dir",
   "note": "`from dotmac_kernel.migrations import versions_dir as kernel_versions_dir` on line 31. SEVEN distributions in that file each publish `versions_dir` and Platform prefixes every one with its distribution, so the local name is Platform's naming scheme rather than anything the Kernel published. This is the sharpest instance of the defect v2 closes: stored as `kernel_versions_dir`, the fact was indistinguishable from any other distribution's `versions_dir` aliased the same way."
  },
  {
